<script>(function(){var P=[["Copán","/city/copan","City","c. 900 BCE – c. 900 CE","Copán is an archaeological site of the Maya civilization in the Copán Department of western Honduras, occupied for more than two thousand years and the capital of a major Classic period kingdom from the 5th to the 9th century CE."],["Jin dynasty (1115-1234)","/empire/jin-dynasty-1115-1234","State","1115 CE – 1234 CE","The empire of the Jurchen people, who overthrew the Khitan Liao, drove the Song from northern China and ruled it until the Mongol conquest of 1234."],["Jericho","/city/jericho","City","c. 9500 BCE – present","Jericho is a city in the Jordan Valley of the West Bank, beside a spring, where archaeologists have found more than 20 successive settlements, the first dating to about 9500 BCE, and where the Hebrew Bible places a siege led by Joshua."],["Chenla","/empire/chenla","State","550 CE – 802 CE","The Chinese name for the Khmer principalities of pre-Angkorian Cambodia, which broke from Funan, absorbed it, split into Land and Water Chenla after 707 and ended with the Khmer Empire in 802."],["Meroë","/city/meroe","City","c. 591 BCE – c. 350 CE","Meroë was an ancient city on the east bank of the Nile in Sudan, the southern capital of the Kingdom of Kush from around 590 BCE until the 4th century CE, and the site of more than two hundred pyramids."],["Assyrian Empire","/empire/assyrian-empire","State","2025 BCE – 609 BCE","The Neo-Assyrian Empire became the most feared military power of its age, perfecting siege warfare and using terror as a deliberate tool of rule. At its height it stretched from Egypt to western Iran."],["Addis Ababa","/city/addis-ababa","City","1886 CE – present","Addis Ababa is the capital and largest city of Ethiopia, standing high in the Ethiopian Highlands at the foot of Mount Entoto. It was founded in 1886 by Empress Taytu Betul and Menelik II and became the imperial capital in 1889."],["Brunei Sultanate","/empire/brunei-sultanate","State","1368 CE – 2025 CE","A Malay sultanate of northern Borneo which in the 16th century ruled coasts from Sarawak to Manila and survives as the independent state of Brunei."],["Mumbai","/city/mumbai","City","c. 250 BCE – present","Mumbai, also called Bombay, is a port city on the Konkan coast of western India, built on an archipelago of seven islands, ruled in turn by Indian dynasties, sultanates, the Portuguese and the British, and now the capital of Maharashtra."],["Han Dynasty","/empire/han-dynasty","State","206 BCE – 220 CE","The Han Dynasty (206 BCE-220 CE) shaped Chinese civilisation for two millennia, and China's majority ethnic group still calls itself Han in its honour. The Silk Road opened during Han expansion into Central Asia."],["Seville","/city/seville","City","c. 750 BCE – present","Seville is a city on the lower Guadalquivir in south-western Spain, founded in the 8th century BCE or earlier as a Tartessian settlement, later the Roman Hispalis, a taifa capital, an Almohad capital and the port of the Spanish Empire's American trade."],["Mataram Sultanate","/empire/mataram-sultanate","State","1587 CE – 1755 CE","The great inland Javanese sultanate of Sultan Agung, which ruled most of Java before dividing into Surakarta and Yogyakarta in 1755."],["Angkor","/city/angkor","City","889 CE – c. 1431 CE","Angkor, also called Yasodharapura, was the capital of the Khmer Empire in present-day Cambodia, founded under Yasovarman in 889 and the centre of a vast network of temples, reservoirs and canals until its sack by Ayutthaya around 1431."],["Numidia","/empire/numidia","State","202 BCE – 46 BCE","The united Berber kingdom of Masinissa and Jugurtha, Rome's powerful ally and then enemy in North Africa."],["Seoul","/city/seoul","City","18 BCE – present","Seoul is the capital and largest city of South Korea, on the Han River in the north-west of the country. Baekje founded its capital in the area in 18 BCE, and Seoul became the capital of the Joseon dynasty in 1394."],["Free and Hanseatic City of Hamburg","/empire/free-and-hanseatic-city-of-hamburg","State","1189 CE – 2025 CE","Elbe port that grew from a Carolingian fort into the Hanseatic League's North Sea gateway and remains a self-governing city-state of Germany today."],["Antioch","/city/antioch","City","300 BCE – present","Antioch was a city on the Orontes River in northern Syria, on the site of modern Antakya in Turkey. Founded in 300 BCE by Seleucus I, it was a Seleucid capital, the capital of Roman Syria and the centre of a Crusader principality."],["Samos","/empire/samos","State","1000 BCE – 129 BCE","Ionian island state that under the tyrant Polycrates became the leading naval power of the Aegean and built the famous Tunnel of Eupalinos."],["Berlin","/city/berlin","City","c. 1237 CE – present","Berlin is a city on the Spree river in north-eastern Germany, founded in the 13th century by German merchants as the twin towns of Berlin and Cölln, and since then a capital of Brandenburg, Prussia, the German Empire and Germany."],["Lan Xang","/empire/lan-xang","State","1353 CE – 1707 CE","The 'Kingdom of a Million Elephants', founded by Fa Ngum in 1353, which united the Lao lands and is the historic forerunner of modern Laos."],["Hanoi","/city/hanoi","City","1010 CE – present","Hanoi is a city on the Red River in northern Vietnam, established as the capital Thăng Long by the Lý dynasty in 1010, later the capital of French Indochina and of North Vietnam, and now the capital of Vietnam."],["Song Dynasty","/empire/song-dynasty","State","960 CE – 1279 CE","The Song Dynasty introduced the first government-issued paper money, movable-type printing, gunpowder weapons and the magnetic compass at sea, and had one of China's most refined cultures."],["Kyiv","/city/kyiv","City","c. 482 CE – present","Kyiv, also spelt Kiev, is the capital of Ukraine, on both banks of the Dnieper. Traditionally dated to 482 CE, it was the capital of Kievan Rus', then a provincial city under several powers, and a Soviet and Ukrainian capital."],["Khmer Empire","/empire/khmer-empire","State","802 CE – 1431 CE","The Khmer Empire built Angkor Wat, the world's largest religious monument, in the middle of one of the pre-modern world's largest urban complexes, which a large network of reservoirs and canals sustained."],["Amsterdam","/city/amsterdam","City","1275 CE – present","Amsterdam is a city on the Amstel river in North Holland, first recorded in 1275 as a settlement by a dam, which became a major trading port of the 17th century and is now the capital of the Netherlands."],["Awadh State","/empire/awadh-state","State","1722 CE – 1856 CE","A Mughal province in North India that its nawabs turned into an independent kingdom, then a British protectorate, until the East India Company annexed it in 1856."],["Anuradhapura","/city/anuradhapura","City","c. 900 BCE – present","Anuradhapura is a city in the north central plain of Sri Lanka, on the Malwathu Oya, settled from about the 10th century BCE, the long-serving ancient capital of the Sinhalese and a centre of Theravada Buddhism."],["Kingdom of Navarre","/empire/kingdom-of-navarre","State","824 CE – 1841 CE","The Basque Pyrenean kingdom of Pamplona, which under Sancho III dominated Christian Spain and kept its own laws until 1841."],["Merv","/city/merv","City","c. 550 BCE – 1789 CE","Merv was an Iranian city of Central Asia on the Silk Road, on the Murghab river near present-day Mary in Turkmenistan, first founded in the 6th century BCE and razed for the last time in 1788 and 1789."],["New France","/empire/new-france","State","1534 CE – 1763 CE","France’s North American empire, stretching from the St Lawrence through the Great Lakes to the Gulf of Mexico, and the origin of French-speaking Canada."],["Kolkata","/city/kolkata","City","1690 CE – present","Kolkata, known as Calcutta until 2001, is a city on the Hooghly River in eastern India, grown from three villages after the East India Company settled there in 1690, and the capital of British India until 1911."],["Seljuk Empire","/empire/seljuk-empire","State","1037 CE – 1194 CE","The Seljuk Turks took Baghdad in 1055 as protectors of the Abbasid caliph and crushed the Byzantines at Manzikert in 1071. Their advance into Anatolia prompted the Byzantine appeal for help that launched the First Crusade."],["Rome","/city/rome","City","c. 753 BCE – present","Rome is the capital and largest city of Italy, on the Tiber in Lazio. Traditionally founded in 753 BCE, it was capital of a kingdom, a republic and an empire, then seat of the popes."],["Macedonian Empire","/empire/macedonian-empire","State","336 BCE – 323 BCE","Alexander the Great's eleven-year campaign created one of the largest empires of antiquity and spread Greek culture from Egypt to India."],["Constantinople","/city/constantinople","City","c. 657 BCE – present (now Istanbul)","Constantinople is a city on the Bosphorus in south-eastern Europe, settled by Greek colonists as Byzantium around 657 BCE, refounded by Constantine as Constantinople, capital of the Roman, Byzantine and Ottoman empires, and now Istanbul."],["Sidon","/empire/sidon","State","1500 BCE – 332 BCE","A Phoenician port with two harbours on the Lebanese coast, famed for its glass and purple dye, mother city of Tyre by its own claim, and under Persian rule the paramount city of Phoenicia."],["Aleppo","/city/aleppo","City","c. 2300 BCE – present","Aleppo is a city in northern Syria, on the Queiq River about 120 km from the Mediterranean, first recorded in the third millennium BCE and for centuries a trading city between the Mediterranean and Mesopotamia."],["Jolof Empire","/empire/jolof-empire","State","1300 CE – 1549 CE","The Jolof Empire united the Wolof peoples of Senegal in one of West Africa's early confederacies, controlling trade between the coast and the interior."],["Lahore","/city/lahore","City","c. 982 CE – present","Lahore is a city on the Ravi River in the Punjab of Pakistan, first named in a document of 982, a capital of the Ghaznavids, the Mughals under Akbar and the Sikh Empire, and now the capital of Pakistan's province of Punjab."],["Aksumite Empire","/empire/aksumite-empire","State","100 CE – 940 CE","One of antiquity's great trading powers, Aksum controlled the Red Sea trade routes and was among the first states to adopt Christianity. Several of its towering granite stelae, often called obelisks, still stand today."],["Damascus","/city/damascus","City","c. 2500 BCE – present","Damascus is the capital of Syria, on a plateau watered by the Barada River below the Anti-Lebanon mountains. First settled in the 3rd millennium BCE, it was an Aramaean capital, a Roman city and the capital of the Umayyad Caliphate."],["Republic of Bolivia","/empire/republic-of-bolivia","State","1825 CE – 2025 CE","The landlocked Andean republic named after Simón Bolívar, born from Upper Peru in 1825 and refounded as a plurinational state in 2009."],["Bangkok","/city/bangkok","City","c. 1400 CE – present","Bangkok is the capital and largest city of Thailand, in the delta of the Chao Phraya River, which grew from a customs outpost of Ayutthaya in the 15th century into the seat of two capitals, Thonburi and Rattanakosin."],["Kingdom of Denmark","/empire/kingdom-of-denmark","State","936 CE – 2025 CE","One of the world’s oldest continuing monarchies, whose kings once ruled England, Norway and the Baltic approaches from Jelling and Copenhagen."],["Barcelona","/city/barcelona","City","c. 15 BCE – present","Barcelona is a city on the north-eastern coast of Spain, on the Mediterranean between the Llobregat and Besòs rivers, settled by an Iberian people, made the Roman colony of Barcino, later the seat of the Counts of Barcelona and now the capital of Catalonia."],["Duchy of Normandy","/empire/duchy-of-normandy","State","911 CE – 1204 CE","The Viking settlement on the lower Seine that became one of Europe’s best-run principalities and launched the Norman conquest of England."],["Kraków","/city/krakow","City","c. 700 CE – present","Kraków is a city on the Vistula in the Lesser Poland region of southern Poland, a fortified settlement from about the 8th century, the seat of Polish monarchs from 1038 to 1596 and today the second-largest city of Poland."],["Chios","/empire/chios","State","1000 BCE – 86 BCE","Rich Ionian island state famed for its wine and mastic, a leading naval power of the Aegean and home of the Homeridae, who claimed descent from Homer."],["Lisbon","/city/lisbon","City","c. 800 BCE – present","Lisbon is the capital of Portugal, on the northern shore of the Tagus estuary in the west of the Iberian Peninsula, an Iron Age and Roman port that became the seat of an Atlantic trading empire."],["County of Toulouse","/empire/county-of-toulouse","State","778 CE – 1271 CE","Great principality of southern France, heart of Occitan culture and troubadour poetry, destroyed by the Albigensian Crusade."],["Florence","/city/florence","City","59 BCE – present","Florence is a city on the Arno in Tuscany, Italy, founded by the Romans in 59 BCE as a colony for army veterans, later a trading and banking commune, the seat of the Medici and a birthplace of the Italian Renaissance."],["Inca Empire","/empire/inca-empire","State","1438 CE – 1533 CE","The largest empire of the pre-Columbian Americas, Tawantinsuyu stretched some 4,000 km along the Andes, linked by roads and run without money or writing."],["Djenné","/city/djenne","City","c. 200 BCE – present","Djenné is a town in the Inland Niger Delta of central Mali, on the floodplain between the Niger and Bani rivers, grown from an urban settlement first occupied around 200 BCE into a trading and Islamic learning centre linked to Timbuktu."],["Kingdom of Sicily","/empire/kingdom-of-sicily","State","1130 CE – 1816 CE","Southern Italy's Norman kingdom, famed for its Arab-Byzantine-Latin court culture, which after 1282 continued as the island realm of Sicily until 1816."],["Kairouan","/city/kairouan","City","c. 670 CE – present","Kairouan is a city in central Tunisia, founded by the Umayyads around 670 as a military post for the conquest of the West, and later the capital of the Aghlabids and the Zirids and a centre of Islamic learning."],["County of Hohenzollern","/empire/county-of-hohenzollern","State","1204 CE – 1576 CE","Swabian county of the Zollern counts, the Catholic home branch of the dynasty that later ruled Brandenburg, Prussia and Germany."],["Delhi","/city/delhi","City","1052 CE – present","Delhi is a city on the Yamuna river in northern India, with a recorded history from the Tomara rulers of the 11th century, the capital of the Delhi Sultanate and the Mughal Empire, and now of the Republic of India."],["Grand Duchy of Tuscany","/empire/grand-duchy-of-tuscany","State","1569 CE – 1859 CE","The Medici and then Habsburg-Lorraine state of Tuscany, patron of Galileo and a pioneer of Enlightenment reform, including abolition of the death penalty."],["Havana","/city/havana","City","1519 CE – present","Havana is the capital and largest city of Cuba, on the island’s northern coast, settled by the Spanish at its present site in 1519 and long a treasure-fleet port, a fortress city, a slave-trade port and a republican capital."],["Kingdom of Magadha","/empire/kingdom-of-magadha","State","600 BCE – 345 BCE","The kingdom of south Bihar that conquered its rivals one by one and became the core of the Nanda and Maurya empires."]],d=Math.floor(Date.now()/864e5),p=P[d%P.length],a=document.getElementById("hub-pick");if(a){a.href=p[1];var im=document.createElement("img");im.src="/logos/thumbs/"+encodeURIComponent(p[0]).replace(/'/g,"%27")+".png";im.alt="";im.width=64;im.height=64;a.querySelector(".hub-pick-img").appendChild(im);a.querySelector(".hub-pick-k").textContent="Today\u2019s pick \u00b7 "+p[2]+(p[3]?" \u00b7 "+p[3]:"");a.querySelector(".hub-pick-n").textContent=p[0];a.querySelector(".hub-pick-d").textContent=p[4];}var b=document.getElementById("hub-surprise"),P=["/city/","/empire/"];if(b)b.addEventListener("click",function(){function go(){if(typeof SEARCH_PROFILES==="undefined")return;var a=SEARCH_PROFILES.filter(function(r){return P.some(function(p){return r[1].indexOf(p)===0})});if(a.length)location.href=a[Math.floor(Math.random()*a.length)][1]}if(typeof SEARCH_PROFILES!=="undefined")return go();var sc=document.createElement("script");sc.src=(typeof SEARCH_PROFILES_SRC!=="undefined"?SEARCH_PROFILES_SRC:"/search-profiles.js");sc.onload=go;sc.onerror=go;document.head.appendChild(sc)});})();</script>
